* ATmega328P (Arduino UNO): fan regulation, NTC thermistor + L298N + DC motor
* Run from this folder:  ngspice ventilo_test.cir
* Firmware: ../firmware/ventilo.hex (make -C ../firmware)
* The NTC warms up from 20 degC at 100 degC/s (accelerated): the motor starts
* at 25 degC (30 %) and reaches 100 % at 35 degC.

* Model generated for this firmware:
*   python3 ../tools/make_atmega328p_lib.py --relative --hex ../firmware/ventilo.hex \
*       --so ../build/mcu_cosim.so --i2c= -o atmega328p_ventilo.lib
.include atmega328p_ventilo.lib
.include ../kicad/ntc.lib
.include ../kicad/motor.lib

*      D0  D1  D2  D3  D4  D5  D6  D7  D8  D9  D10  D11  D12  D13  A0  A1  A2  A3  A4  A5
X1     nd0 txd nd2 nd3 nd4 nd5 ena in1 in2 nb1 nb2  nb3  nb4  nb5  ntc na1 na2 na3 na4 na5 ATMEGA328P

* Divider: 10 kohm to 5 V, NTC to GND
R1 v5 ntc 10k
XT ntc 0 NTC10K params: T0=20 RATE=100
C1 ntc 0 100n

*      SENSE_A OUT1 OUT2 VS IN1 ENA IN2 GND VSS IN3 ENB IN4 OUT3 OUT4 SENSE_B
XU2    0       m1   m2   v9 in1 ena in2 0   v5  0   0   0   o3   o4   0       L298N
*      P  N  SPEED
XM     m1 m2 speed MOTOR_DC

V5 v5 0 5
V9 v9 0 9
Rtx txd 0 100k

.control
tran 2u 0.3
meas tran vitesse avg v(speed) from=0.27 to=0.3
plot v(speed) v(xt.temp)/10 v(ena)
.endc
.end
